# A finite, read-only resource measurement for one exact systemd unit.
# By default yesh stores records below ~/.local/.yesh/resources/<unit> and
# creates only that user-owned directory tree when needed. An explicit
# `save to $state_dir` path can be used for a different layout.
#
# Run with --plan first. The unit must already exist and be readable by the
# selected systemd manager. A scheduled measurement can be repeated by an
# external systemd timer; yesh itself remains a finite foreground command.

# The retention directive belongs to this measurement and keeps a 24-hour
# sliding history for the selected unit.
measure service user api.service for 10s every 2s:
    save to state
    keep history for 24h
summarize service user api.service from state since 1h
